{"parentUuid":"130f83f9-47aa-43b6-9d0e-6a2ca73f7e74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGVdTbaG2YzxRhotNgH1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xk8oVVLS4qBDuBCF1AzvAk","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.17440v1","prompt":"What does the paper say about how rain looks in real nighttime images: where rain streaks are visible relative to light sources, how their brightness depends on the illumination/background, and why uniformly added synthetic rain looks unrealistic? Quote the key sentences (short) and list the figure numbers/URLs of figures showing real nighttime rain images."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2451,"cache_read_input_tokens":219924,"output_tokens":395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":197},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2451,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":219924,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2451},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Xk8oVVLS4qBDuBCF1AzvAk":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.17440v1","prompt":"What does the paper say about how rain looks in real nighttime images: where rain streaks are visible relative to light sources, how their brightness depends on the illumination/background, and why uniformly added synthetic rain looks unrealistic? Quote the key sentences (short) and list the figure numbers/URLs of figures showing real nighttime rain images."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"78a0943c-3446-4727-be7a-cbb43996ab78","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGVdT6ZXK5Qsqb4RNdYQ","requestRef":"d266b8fc-eac3-46a6-a9b0-a7c67530caab","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fb79f13-a319-4792-9040-37afe726560a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:34:17.557Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"6fb79f13-a319-4792-9040-37afe726560a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xk8oVVLS4qBDuBCF1AzvAk","type":"tool_result","content":"**How rain appears at night**\n\n- Rain is tied to light sources. The paper says \"rain in nighttime scenes is only visible near light sources and is not noticeable in low-illumination areas.\" (Sec. 3.1)\n- Rain is also hidden in the brightest areas: \"Rain is not only invisible in low-illumination areas but also in excessively high-illumination areas\" (Sec. 3.2).\n- Rain brightness depends on the background. Rain \"often reflects light from artificial sources, creating high-contrast patterns that stand out sharply against the dark background\" (Sec. 1). Paraphrasing Appendix B, rain streaks noticeably shift local illumination, which is why the Y channel shows the largest rain-related histogram change at night.\n\n**Why uniform synthetic rain looks unrealistic**\n\n- Earlier datasets add rain uniformly: \"random rain masks are added linearly to nighttime backgrounds\" (Sec. 1). The authors say this \"naturally leads to inadequate realism and harmony in the visual appearance\" (Sec. 1).\n- Paraphrasing Sec. 1, the authors argue uniform rain ignores the fact that real rain visibility varies with lighting, so it creates a domain gap with real images.\n\n**Figures showing real nighttime rain images**\n\n- Figure 6: real-world nighttime rainy images from RealRain-1k. Input paths: `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig6/1/01Input.jpg` and `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig6/2/01Input.jpg`\n- Figure 8: generalization results on real-world nighttime rainy images. Input path: `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig7/Input.jpg`\n- Figure 9: visual comparisons on real-world nighttime rainy images. Input path: `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig8/Input.jpg`\n- Figure 13(d): example \"Real\" images from HQ-NightRain (Appendix F). Path: `2510.17440v1/figs/Dataset_show/Real.jpg`\n\nThese paths are relative to the arXiv HTML page for 2510.17440v1. The page does not describe these real images in detail beyond these captions.\n\n[WebFetch note: this page's text is 106802 characters long and the answer above covers only characters 0 to 100000; the final 6802 were not read — to read on, call WebFetch again with the same url and offset: 100000.]"}]},"uuid":"cd135586-dd0a-4b12-8e46-5bb751d09486","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:34:29.158Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":507624,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**How rain appears at night**\n\n- Rain is tied to light sources. The paper says \"rain in nighttime scenes is only visible near light sources and is not noticeable in low-illumination areas.\" (Sec. 3.1)\n- Rain is also hidden in the brightest areas: \"Rain is not only invisible in low-illumination areas but also in excessively high-illumination areas\" (Sec. 3.2).\n- Rain brightness depends on the background. Rain \"often reflects light from artificial sources, creating high-contrast patterns that stand out sharply against the dark background\" (Sec. 1). Paraphrasing Appendix B, rain streaks noticeably shift local illumination, which is why the Y channel shows the largest rain-related histogram change at night.\n\n**Why uniform synthetic rain looks unrealistic**\n\n- Earlier datasets add rain uniformly: \"random rain masks are added linearly to nighttime backgrounds\" (Sec. 1). The authors say this \"naturally leads to inadequate realism and harmony in the visual appearance\" (Sec. 1).\n- Paraphrasing Sec. 1, the authors argue uniform rain ignores the fact that real rain visibility varies with lighting, so it creates a domain gap with real images.\n\n**Figures showing real nighttime rain images**\n\n- Figure 6: real-world nighttime rainy images from RealRain-1k. Input paths: `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig6/1/01Input.jpg` and `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig6/2/01Input.jpg`\n- Figure 8: generalization results on real-world nighttime rainy images. Input path: `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig7/Input.jpg`\n- Figure 9: visual comparisons on real-world nighttime rainy images. Input path: `2510.17440v1/figs/Fig8/Input.jpg`\n- Figure 13(d): example \"Real\" images from HQ-NightRain (Appendix F). Path: `2510.17440v1/figs/Dataset_show/Real.jpg`\n\nThese paths are relative to the arXiv HTML page for 2510.17440v1. The page does not describe these real images in detail beyond these captions.\n\n[WebFetch note: this page's text is 106802 characters long and the answer above covers only characters 0 to 100000; the final 6802 were not read — to read on, call WebFetch again with the same url and offset: 100000.]","durationMs":10936,"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.17440v1"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"78a0943c-3446-4727-be7a-cbb43996ab78","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"REDACTED","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"REDACTED","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6fb79f13-a319-4792-9040-37afe726560a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
