{"parentUuid":"7ec6d9b3-3f3d-42a4-8109-b1cc98708576","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PyidV3UVnvu3fkGmz4koQS","type":"tool_result","content":"[[\"qa01_lane_start\",18.52,609,3494],[\"qa04_street\",21.57,705,4270]]\n7:**Mission 1 — Saint-Clair, at dusk.** Normandy, July 1944, evening, rain.\n19:The look is built for realism at dusk in the rain: every model carries baked\n21:steel, hessian, wool, bark and moss, with occlusion, grime and rain streaks\n32:walls, wrecks and crates the grain of their surface, behind\n35:shifts with parallax as you walk past, seen up close through rain beaded on\n38:shape of the window with its glazing bars across it, the rain in front of\n44:lamps and the glow of the sky, broken by rain rings the size of a\n45:raindrop's, many and quick (further off the rain only roughens the water),\n53:them in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\n72:swing as it drifts, its light hanging in the rain in shafts between the roofs.\n78:soft shadows and their light hangs in the rain between you and them, corners\n80:contrast, sharpening, grain in the shadows — going soft behind whatever you\n127:  * `terrain.js` heightfield + splat material · `world.js` colliders, rays,\n153:  * `distance.js` the countryside beyond the level: a terrain ring of fields\n159:    distance across and along them, from which the terrain cuts two ruts a\n162:  * `ponds.js` rainwater in the shell craters (the level's `craters`): a\n167:    breadth from its edge, from its depth in the ground map, rain rings, no\n171:    terrain mesh's own splat: grass, stones and fallen wood (none on roads,\n184:    generated metre of surface grain in world space from three sides,\n186:    stands; rain running down walls within ~24 m in","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d8b0c18-1645-43f2-ae1b-9e12bdcd98ed","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:40:34.908Z","toolUseResult":{"stdou