{"parentUuid":"181f520f-3c26-4ade-8928-e4271199c4cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGXCKDpS23dJw8i85Myx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TrsRqtbDCpZ751WrVyivEN","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    a lamp or a fire beyond them, a drop sending on most of the light it\n    catches as a lens does (a Henyey-Greenstein lobe);","new_string":"    a lamp or a fire beyond them, a drop sending on most of the light it\n    catches as a lens does (a Henyey-Greenstein lobe); and the rain in the\n    lamplight - round the four nearest lamps and fires within 30 m and the\n    two nearest flashes, a box of drops of its own (some 1,100 on high)\n    falling through the light, seen only by the light they catch, each a\n    tiny bright image of it: a cone of glittering streaks under a lamp's\n    cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, a muzzle's or a shell's flash\n    lighting the rain round it for its few frames (the player's own, at the\n    eye, hardly), none under a roof or an eave (the top of what is over\n    each of 6 x 6 cells of the box, from the world's rays, once per place);"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5895,"cache_read_input_tokens":365910,"output_tokens":1606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":428},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5895,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1606,"cache_read_input_tokens":365910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5895},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TrsRqtbDCpZ751WrVyivEN":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    a lamp or a fire beyond them, a drop sending on most of the light it\n    catches as a lens does (a Henyey-Greenstein lobe);","new_string":"    a lamp or a fire beyond them, a drop sending on most of the light it\n    catches as a lens does (a Henyey-Greenstein lobe); and the rain in the\n    lamplight - round the four nearest lamps and fires within 30 m and the\n    two nearest flashes, a box of drops of its own (some 1,100 on high)\n    falling through the light, seen only by the light they catch, each a\n    tiny bright image of it: a cone of glittering streaks under a lamp's\n    cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, a muzzle's or a shell's flash\n    lighting the rain round it for its few frames (the player's own, at the\n    eye, hardly), none under a roof or an eave (the top of what is over\n    each of 6 x 6 cells of the box, from the world's rays, once per place);"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8c4111fb-4911-46fa-974a-d940d792f633","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGXCJomnGkokWerisXPr","requestRef":"e7f680cd-528a-4d57-9dc9-199003a8191c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8991c8f1-f3be-4536-8da3-f902d6a99d5f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:54:54.597Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"8991c8f1-f3be-4536-8da3-f902d6a99d5f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGXCKDpS23dJw8i85Myx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RZBVvxb3w1gVLKKtQCzDUU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js fun/hedgerow/js/lights.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain glitters in the lamplight\n\nAt night rain is all but invisible except near a light, where it shows\nas dense, bright streaks (the street-lamp photographs in arXiv\n2510.17440). The near rain's 9,000 drops stand for the rain in the dark\nand are far too few to show that, so the lamps, fires and flashes near\nthe eye now get rain of their own.\n\nAround each of the four nearest lamps and fires within 30 m, and the two\nnearest flashes, there is a box of about 1,100 drops (on high) falling\nthrough its light. Each is seen only by the light it catches, as a tiny\nbright image of the light, brighter than the haze around it and capped\nso it never blinds. This gives a cone of glittering streaks under a\nlamp's cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, and a burst of lit rain\nfor the few frames of a muzzle or shell flash. The player's own muzzle,\nat the eye, is damped because a real flash lasts about a millisecond.\n\nNone fall under a roof or an eave: for each light's 6 x 6 cells, the\ntop of whatever is over the cell comes from the world's rays, once per\nplace. The drops keep their places in the world as the box follows its\nlight, so a fire's sway does not drag the rain. Flashes have their own\nslots and are marked as flashes in lights.js, so gunfire never takes a\nlamp's rain away. Cost is within frame-to-frame noise at the views\nmeasured (about +0.5 ms at most, close to a fire).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the lamplight rain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5895,"cache_read_input_tokens":365910,"output_tokens":1606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":428},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5895,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1606,"cache_read_input_tokens":365910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5895},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RZBVvxb3w1gVLKKtQCzDUU":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js fun/hedgerow/js/lights.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain glitters in the lamplight\n\nAt night rain is all but invisible except near a light, where it shows\nas dense, bright streaks (the street-lamp photographs in arXiv\n2510.17440). The near rain's 9,000 drops stand for the rain in the dark\nand are far too few to show that, so the lamps, fires and flashes near\nthe eye now get rain of their own.\n\nAround each of the four nearest lamps and fires within 30 m, and the two\nnearest flashes, there is a box of about 1,100 drops (on high) falling\nthrough its light. Each is seen only by the light it catches, as a tiny\nbright image of the light, brighter than the haze around it and capped\nso it never blinds. This gives a cone of glittering streaks under a\nlamp's cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, and a burst of lit rain\nfor the few frames of a muzzle or shell flash. The player's own muzzle,\nat the eye, is damped because a real flash lasts about a millisecond.\n\nNone fall under a roof or an eave: for each light's 6 x 6 cells, the\ntop of whatever is over the cell comes from the world's rays, once per\nplace. The drops keep their places in the world as the box follows its\nlight, so a fire's sway does not drag the rain. Flashes have their own\nslots and are marked as flashes in lights.js, so gunfire never takes a\nlamp's rain away. Cost is within frame-to-frame noise at the views\nmeasured (about +0.5 ms at most, close to a fire).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the lamplight rain"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01RZBVvxb3w1gVLKKtQCzDUU":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8c4111fb-4911-46fa-974a-d940d792f633","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgGXCJomnGkokWerisXPr","requestRef":"e7f680cd-528a-4d57-9dc9-199003a8191c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a20fe57-d0b9-43db-870b-418811084575","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:55:00.730Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
