{"parentUuid":"3c160377-5d3f-4765-bf66-8cc75c60c763","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"17b7ed16-a101-4402-afdd-06026f97016b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FcdVjkDcbg9PjcaQYaPHBy","type":"tool_result","content":"total 88\ndrwx------@ 3 vojta  staff     96 Oct 22 01:52 .\ndrwx------@ 3 vojta  staff     96 Oct 21 14:44 ..\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 vojta  staff  44206 Oct 22 04:18 hedgerow-grass-session.md\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, fifth:\n- Tried and reverted (not committed): reflections in upright window glass. Debug colouring found the\n  baked panes at wet roughness 0.16-0.24 (upright); the weather patch told ssr.js only about level\n  water (mirrorAlpha via mWetUp), and ssr.js drops non-level normals, downward rays and hits not\n  above the water. A glass range in the scene alpha (0.5-0.75, glass = upright mirror) plus ssr.js\n  and volumetric.js reading it worked technically, but A/Bs from head-on, grazing and fire-aligned\n  views showed nothing concentrated in the panes (screen space: the head-on reflection is behind the\n  camera; at grazing angles the panes mirror the dark houses opposite). Not worth the risk.\n- 87bdf2f5 rain lands on what it meets first: weather.js landY casts down from y + 30 through\n  world colliders (SHOT, noTerrain, noWater; ignore t < 0.01 = started inside), takes an upward top\n  above the ground; main.js passes world. Crowns/rings now on crate lids etc. 4400 rays = 0.9 ms CPU\n  (per second of splashes); 19% of random street spots land on a top (mostly roofs).\n- Looked at the lane, a field and the forest track: very dark - exposure/readability at night stays\n  the user's call (gap 8).\n  Not seen in a real browser window: headless renders only.\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, sixth:\n  References without the pane: hl.mjs gained `view <url> <out.png>` (a throwaway headless tab,\n  Page.captureScreenshot, closed; screenshots kept in scratch only while comparing, then deleted).\n  MoH: Airborne LP (lparchive.org/Medal-of-Honor-Airborne -> YouTube IDs; Neptune mission IMb3E2g6u40,\n  skill drops xbBcVf2K5ZY): img.youtube.com/vi/<id>/hq1|hq2|hq3.jpg are frames at 25/50/75%. Neptune\n  is daytime/overcast: trenches with concertina and barbed-wire posts, stained concrete, dirt clods\n  thrown by blasts, the parachute drop. Compared with our trench/bunker area (night, very dark).\n- fd184b5e concertina (wire.js): along each barbed_wire prop (levelBuild passes {x,y,z,yaw,len from\n  m.box}), a coil r ~0.4 m, PITCH 0.2, 20 samples/loop, 5-sided tube, alternating loop tilt\n  0.42 cos(a/2) (crossing diamonds), sag, lean; vertex shader widens to max(2.8 mm, dist * 0.0011).\n  Gotchas: tube winding was inside-out at first (only the far inner side drew - visible only with\n  emissive); rust #6e5a48 + metal 0.35 matched the night ground (10.3 vs 11.7 grey levels under it);\n  a white matte test proved the lighting; galvanised #8a8378 m0.45 r0.36 reads up close by a light,\n  a faint tangle at 3-4 m in the dark forest.\n  Checked: low/medium/high compile, 9 node checks, merge-tree clean. Headless renders only.\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, seventh:\n- 2a1466a3 boot prints (prints.js + atmosphere.js 'boot' decal kind, pinned 1100, 993 placed): files\n  along LEVEL.lines LANE (3) and TRACK (2), stride 0.72 m, L/R 0.11 m either side, 22% skipped,\n  variants 0 L / 1 R / 2 scuffed / 3 water-filled, only where terrain.surfaceAt === 'mud'; pin()/put()\n  take an optional `angle` (a turn a carries the decal's up = world +x to (cos a, -sin a) on a floor).\n  Painter: decal up = canvas down (rows run up v), so the toe is drawn towards +y. In the dark lane:\n  dark marks; by flare light: sole, heel and rim read. Checks: presets, 9 node checks, merge clean.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9988fb3b-42e0-4dcb-835a-803462aa8f53","timestamp":"2026-10-22T02:55:23.558Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"total 88\ndrwx------@ 3 vojta  staff     96 Oct 22 01:52 .\ndrwx------@ 3 vojta  staff     96 Oct 21 14:44 ..\n-rw-r--r--