{"parentUuid":"4bc56950-b0bc-464c-a33e-0ad3e7818e5c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGYQ9AHo3BfYNkgph6Sc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B7cT3RmmGqwrrFHYcw63iU","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    fires as flame: five billboards over the breadth of each near fire,\n    rising two to three metres out of the wreck, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core), `plumes.js` (each","new_string":"    fires as flame: five billboards over the breadth of each near fire,\n    rising two to three metres out of the wreck, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core; hidden pixels thrown\n    away before the noise is worked out; a house burning through and\n    through - the roofless ruin at the village entry - has flame all\n    over its floor and up in the charred joists of the floor above (the\n    level's `blaze`: more flames, each fainter, with embers and sparks\n    but no smoke or plume of their own, and a light by the door), so its\n    door and every window blaze and the light pours out over the wet\n    cobbles), `plumes.js` (each"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":483197,"output_tokens":1154,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":735,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1154,"cache_read_input_tokens":483197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":735},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01B7cT3RmmGqwrrFHYcw63iU":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    fires as flame: five billboards over the breadth of each near fire,\n    rising two to three metres out of the wreck, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core), `plumes.js` (each","new_string":"    fires as flame: five billboards over the breadth of each near fire,\n    rising two to three metres out of the wreck, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core; hidden pixels thrown\n    away before the noise is worked out; a house burning through and\n    through - the roofless ruin at the village entry - has flame all\n    over its floor and up in the charred joists of the floor above (the\n    level's `blaze`: more flames, each fainter, with embers and sparks\n    but no smoke or plume of their own, and a light by the door), so its\n    door and every window blaze and the light pours out over the wet\n    cobbles), `plumes.js` (each"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"21399d0f-eb39-402b-bf2f-93a0433dfcde","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGYQ8U7v9XZBKWd2G8gK","requestRef":"aec4fa7f-3b9d-4d2a-adda-305f2195e6ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc4dc969-9ee2-4c1c-9491-f8e3937ffcb8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:10:37.911Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"cc4dc969-9ee2-4c1c-9491-f8e3937ffcb8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGYQ9AHo3BfYNkgph6Sc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BJNck62sgSM29PRRUopxbK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git status --short && git diff --stat && git add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/flames.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/levels/saint-clair.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the ruin at the village entry burns through and through\n\nCoD Vanguard's Normandy night (\"Operation Tonga\") is lit by whole\nbuildings on fire. Our ruin \"with a fire\" had one small fire at ground\nlevel deep inside its walls, so from the street it read as a dark shell.\n\nThe level now spreads flame over the ruin's floor and up into the charred\njoists of the floor above. A prop's new `blaze` list holds flames in the\nmodel's own frame. They are extra flame bodies on the debris-fire list,\neach with a fainter flame gain, carrying embers and sparks but no smoke,\nno plume and no glow on the clouds of their own. A light of their own\nstands by the door. The ruin's own fire is bigger (`fireSize`). Its door\nand every window blaze, flames lick out of the upper window, and the\nfirelight pours over the wet cobbles.\n\nflames.js: fires can set their own gain, up to 16 nearby fires are drawn\n(was 10), and pixels hidden behind the scene are discarded before the\nnoise is computed. Every fire got cheaper, by about 1-2 ms at the ruin,\nand the blaze costs about 0.5 ms standing in front of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -4","description":"Commit the burning ruin"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":483197,"output_tokens":1154,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":735,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1154,"cache_read_input_tokens":483197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":735},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BJNck62sgSM29PRRUopxbK":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git diff --stat && git add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/flames.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/levels/saint-clair.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the ruin at the village entry burns through and through\n\nCoD Vanguard's Normandy night (\"Operation Tonga\") is lit by whole\nbuildings on fire. Our ruin \"with a fire\" had one small fire at ground\nlevel deep inside its walls, so from the street it read as a dark shell.\n\nThe level now spreads flame over the ruin's floor and up into the charred\njoists of the floor above. A prop's new `blaze` list holds flames in the\nmodel's own frame. They are extra flame bodies on the debris-fire list,\neach with a fainter flame gain, carrying embers and sparks but no smoke,\nno plume and no glow on the clouds of their own. A light of their own\nstands by the door. The ruin's own fire is bigger (`fireSize`). Its door\nand every window blaze, flames lick out of the upper window, and the\nfirelight pours over the wet cobbles.\n\nflames.js: fires can set their own gain, up to 16 nearby fires are drawn\n(was 10), and pixels hidden behind the scene are discarded before the\nnoise is computed. Every fire got cheaper, by about 1-2 ms at the ruin,\nand the blaze costs about 0.5 ms standing in front of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -4","description":"Commit the burning ruin"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01BJNck62sgSM29PRRUopxbK":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"21399d0f-eb39-402b-bf2f-93a0433dfcde","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGYQ8U7v9XZBKWd2G8gK","requestRef":"aec4fa7f-3b9d-4d2a-adda-305f2195e6ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2927316b-a4db-4094-a267-94fca0205d37","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:10:43.843Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
