{"parentUuid":"556640c2-ca14-4f60-9651-4a25a98f69b8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>10179446 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a2bf79cc-2b99-4b83-8474-2b6de4b68cc8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:19:09.150Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>10179446 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"b07c008446c23a590500d6b5641a48648928f0fd08a2de272fe6efcca6c0fcad","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Before wiring this in, I need to fix two issues: the snag-point selection logic is unclear, and large crowns would hide the canopy from ground view. I'll adjust the apex to start near the crown's edge on the track side so the silk spills down visibly.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X3i656c9EjBReD95QRR2Bu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='chutes.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"  // where it starts: flat over the crown's top, its apex a little out towards the track, turned and\n  // tipped at random, crumpled a little\n  const cw = cr.c.clone().applyMatrix4(M), ry = cr.r.y * k, rxz = Math.min(cr.r.x, cr.r.z) * k;\n  const apex = cw.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(toward.x * rxz * 0.4, ry + 0.4, toward.z * rxz * 0.4));\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"  // where it starts: lying over the crown, its apex out near the crown's edge on the track's side (so\n  // it spills down that side), turned and tipped at random, crumpled a little\n  const cw = cr.c.clone().applyMatrix4(M), ry = cr.r.y * k, rxz = Math.min(cr.r.x, cr.r.z) * k;\n  const apex = cw.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(toward.x * rxz * 0.68, ry * 0.73 + 0.4, toward.z * rxz * 0.68));\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"\"\"  // snagged: the apex, and on the far side from the track two points of its second ring\n  pinned[0] = 1;\n  for (let j = 0, best = []; j < NS; j++) {\n    const p = id(2, j), d = (P[p * 3] - apex.x) * toward.x + (P[p * 3 + 2] - apex.z) * toward.z;\n    best.push([d, p]);\n    if (j === NS - 1) best.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]).slice(0, 2).forEach(([, q]) => { pinned[q] = 1; });\n  }\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"  // snagged: the apex, and the two points of its second ring furthest from the track\n  pinned[0] = 1;\n  const ring2 = [];\n  for (let j = 0; j < NS; j++) {\n    const p = id(2, j);\n    ring2.push([(P[p * 3] - apex.x) * toward.x + (P[p * 3 + 2] - apex.z) * toward.z, p]);\n  }\n  ring2.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);\n  pinned[ring2[0][1]] = pinned[ring2[1][1]] = 1;\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='main.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"  G.sheets = createSheets(panes, G.world, G.terrain, shared);\n  if (G.sheets) scene.add(G.sheets.mesh);\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"  G.sheets = createSheets(panes, G.world, G.terrain, shared);\n  if (G.sheets) scene.add(G.sheets.mesh);\n  // and parachutes caught in the trees by the forest track (chutes.js)\n  G.chutes = createChutes(built.veg, LEVEL.lines, G.terrain, shared);\n  if (G.chutes) scene.add(G.chutes.group);\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"import { createSheets } from './cloth.js';\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,\"import { createSheets } from './cloth.js';\\nimport { createChutes } from './chutes.js';\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode --check chutes.js && echo syntax-ok; grep -n \"createChutes\" main.js","description":"Fix the apex start and snag points, wire chutes into main.js"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
