{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","id":"a3117f21-eaa0-4a5d-85d3-db92f73a96ec","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:28:12.082Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"b880ec811c15b646f9012e782c42974027e0eddc512cfae1370cf4df924f4f49","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"3e689534-0e68-436d-9f98-34f2f04db81a","keep":675,"tail":["d95a5b1186d368c2af2fa97311e8f75f3c0ac4472bda761f13239a8defdc6c9c","655091d44c9a47d721ec07954f6388dce60c4fd21ee9ece0af9056f08fea420b","7da884304a86a4028a59105469122a8f2b509865a32df8279a3d88e6d774f9eb"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",677,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8512044dd2d7de039febddad06bee1d7b6ece87b6da6f6e777523acd8aa07242"}
{"parentUuid":"ec15845f-d6a0-4895-9cfb-e047959d0383","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGZkDvTA2nNakDBiHq4P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XwjoyWoY87rnmKSthyQdr2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, tenth:\n- Weakest area: the forest half (track, trenches, bunker, camp) - a flat murky mass at night,\n  nothing pale or lit between flares (a flare launched from the forest goes up ~150 m off, east;\n  its light reaches the track in hard white patches).\n- 06597f9f parachutes in the trees (chutes.js; main.js calls createChutes(built.veg,\n  LEVEL.lines, G.terrain, shared) after the sheets). veg.kinds (vegetation.js) gives each placed\n  tree's model + matrix. Picks BROAD trees 5.5-12 m off TRACK, z 300-480, crown bottom < 9 m, 45 m\n  apart (seed 6 -> birch_a 1.9,460.4 / tree_dead 9.1,376.7 / oak_b 2.6,302.9). Crown = ellipsoid\n  from the model's points above 36% height (6-94% spans; x0.62 for birch/dead). Drape: polar net\n  NR 10 x NS 28 + apex, constraints ring/radial/shear/skip-two, slack resisted only 4% (else it\n  holds a dome), apex + two ring-3 points snagged on the crown's track-side flank (lift 0.35-0.55),\n  120 steps x 5 passes, crown/trunk/ground collision with 0.8 clinging, Math.hypot was the cost\n  (995 -> 114-130 ms after sqrt, inlined matrices, 2 collisions per step). Lines: every other skirt\n  point to a meet 3.2-4.6 m below the lowest hem (>= 2.3 m over the ground) + 2 risers, pale tan\n  (dark ones vanished at night). Gust sway on aFree (distance from lying points). 1.6k + 3k tris.\n- References: YouTube \"Tree Landing\" CAvPEzvrbX8 (real paratroopers in a pine; risers straight up\n  into the branches) and MoH Airborne nqrkCvBF5jo frames (plane, Tiger, burning tank + black\n  column); none showed a canopy in a tree. Viewed headless, deleted.\n  Checks: low/medium/high compile (97/147/147, 0 bad, flare shadow passes included), 9 node\n  checks, merge-tree clean. Clip mv_chute.mp4 sent. Not seen in a real browser window.\nEOF\nREDACTED; cd $S && node hl.mjs stop; rm -rf hl-profile; pkill -f \"nocache_server.py 8766\"; sleep 1; lsof -nP -iTCP:8766 -sTCP:LISTEN | head -2; lsof -nP -iTCP:9337 -sTCP:LISTEN | head -2; pgrep -fl \"hl-profile|nocache_server\" | head; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short | head; git log --oneline -1","description":"Note this turn, stop the rig and verify it is down","timeout":60000,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":608044,"output_tokens":1306,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1106,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1306,"cache_read_input_tokens":608044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1106},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XwjoyWoY87rnmKSthyQdr2":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, tenth:\n- Weakest area: the forest half (track, trenches, bunker, camp) - a flat murky mass at night,\n  nothing pale or lit between flares (a flare launched from the forest goes up ~150 m off, east;\n  its light reaches the track in hard white patches).\n- 06597f9f parachutes in the trees (chutes.js; main.js calls createChutes(built.veg,\n  LEVEL.lines, G.terrain, shared) after the sheets). veg.kinds (vegetation.js) gives each placed\n  tree's model + matrix. Picks BROAD trees 5.5-12 m off TRACK, z 300-480, crown bottom < 9 m, 45 m\n  apart (seed 6 -> birch_a 1.9,460.4 / tree_dead 9.1,376.7 / oak_b 2.6,302.9). Crown = ellipsoid\n  from the model's points above 36% height (6-94% spans; x0.62 for birch/dead). Drape: polar net\n  NR 10 x NS 28 + apex, constraints ring/radial/shear/skip-two, slack resisted only 4% (else it\n  holds a dome), apex + two ring-3 points snagged on the crown's track-side flank (lift 0.35-0.55),\n  120 steps x 5 passes, crown/trunk/ground collision with 0.8 clinging, Math.hypot was the cost\n  (995 -> 114-130 ms after sqrt, inlined matrices, 2 collisions per step). Lines: every other skirt\n  point to a meet 3.2-4.6 m below the lowest hem (>= 2.3 m over the ground) + 2 risers, pale tan\n  (dark ones vanished at night). Gust sway on aFree (distance from lying points). 1.6k + 3k tris.\n- References: YouTube \"Tree Landing\" CAvPEzvrbX8 (real paratroopers in a pine; risers straight up\n  into the branches) and MoH Airborne nqrkCvBF5jo frames (plane, Tiger, burning tank + black\n  column); none showed a canopy in a tree. Viewed headless, deleted.\n  Checks: low/medium/high compile (97/147/147, 0 bad, flare shadow passes included), 9 node\n  checks, merge-tree clean. Clip mv_chute.mp4 sent. Not seen in a real browser window.\nEOF\nREDACTED; cd $S && node hl.mjs stop; rm -rf hl-profile; pkill -f \"nocache_server.py 8766\"; sleep 1; lsof -nP -iTCP:8766 -sTCP:LISTEN | head -2; lsof -nP -iTCP:9337 -sTCP:LISTEN | head -2; pgrep -fl \"hl-profile|nocache_server\" | head; cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short | head; git log --oneline -1","description":"Note this turn, stop the rig and verify it is down","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true,"timeout":60000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"70182ac3-3fe9-4a2b-9517-3155b9dbde30","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGZkDPDFw6L1yNw3GBtR"